Now water base improvements: add water depth blooms and foam patchiness. Edit world.js.

First add a water mottling loop after broad mottling loop. Need to know constants available: WATER_DEEP/MID/SHALLOW, rand, BASE, sampleField, WORLD, smoothstep. Yes.

Add:

```js
  // painterly depth blooms inside the water
  for (let i = 0; i < 340; i++) {
    const bx = rand() * BASE;
    const by = rand() * BASE;
    const wx = (bx / BASE) * WORLD;
    const wy = (by / BASE) * WORLD;
    const e = sampleField(height, wx, wy);
    if (e > 0.004) continue;
    const deep = smoothstep(-0.08, -0.5, e);
    const col = deep > 0.45
      ? (rand() < 0.6 ? WATER_DEEP : WATER_MID)
      : (rand() < 0.55 ? WATER_MID : WATER_SHALLOW);
    bctx.globalAlpha = 0.035 + rand() * 0.055;
    bctx.fillStyle = `rgb(${col[0]},${col[1]},${col[2]})`;
    bctx.beginPath();
    const rad = 10 + rand() * 46;
    bctx.ellipse(bx, by, rad, rad * (0.5 + rand() * 0.7), rand() * TAU, 0, TAU);
    bctx.fill();
  }
  bctx.globalAlpha = 1;
```

Wait smoothstep(-0.08, -0.5, e): if edge0 > edge1, util smoothstep may behave weird. Check util smoothstep implementation.

export const TAU = Math.PI * 2;

export const clamp = (v, a, b) => (v < a ? a : v > b ? b : v);
export const lerp = (a, b, t) => a + (b - a) * t;
export const invLerp = (a, b, v) => clamp((v - a) / (b - a), 0, 1);
export const smoothstep = (a, b, v) => {
  const t = clamp((v - a) / (b - a), 0, 1);
  return t * t * (3 - 2 * t);
};
export const mix = (a, b, t) => [
  lerp(a[0], b[0], t),
  lerp(a[1], b[1], t),
  lerp(a[2], b[2], t),
];

